@startuml
!include _style.iuml
' Adapted from reviewed presentation sources: W2-delivery-ledgers, W3-07a; separate SQL commit / relay / consumer
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 17
skinparam ClassStereotypeFontSize 15
skinparam NoteFontSize 16
skinparam LegendFontSize 15
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 135
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 24
hide footbox
hide circle
title DP-2 · lost-send reply, replay and atomic acceptance
autonumber
database "Media DB" as MD $INFRA
participant "sql\ndelivery" as D $INFRA
participant "messaging\nprocessing" as P $PROC
database "Processing DB" as PD $INFRA
note over MD : direct_intake.finalize has committed\npin + Asset + MediaOutbox.
... MediaRepair calls publish_commands → publish_due ...
loop each due outbox row, bounded by limit / deadline
 D -> MD : lock SKIP LOCKED; save claim token; COMMIT
 D ->] : transport.send(queue, body)\n[SQS.send → native send_message]
 alt send reply lost / network error
  D -> MD : fence matching claim token; retain row;\nschedule retry of SAME message_id
 else acknowledged send
  D -> MD : fence matching token; sent_at; next replay; COMMIT
 end
end
... processing-commands delivery / redelivery ...
[-> P : handle_command(factory, message)
group one Processing transaction
 P -> PD : SQL: inbox UUID / hash\n[delivery.sql.accept]
 alt duplicate ID and identical body hash
  P -->[ : False; no domain mutation
 else conflicting body hash
  P -> PD : ROLLBACK; MessageConflict
 else new command
  P -> PD : guard + Job + Attempt + work/result outboxes; COMMIT
  P -->[ : True
 end
end
note over MD,PD
Queue delivery is asynchronous; the relay does not
call Processing directly.
consume_batch / event-source mapping ACK only
committed successful records.
Processing's result outbox → Media inbox/projection
repeats the same local pattern.
end note
@enduml
